{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And I called drought</b> — by way of ellipsis, like: \"because my house which is desolate.\"" "<b>And the meaning of \"and I called\"</b> — and I decree upon the earth until it becomes like bronze." "<b>And upon the mountains</b> — the produce of the mountains, like \"and from the head of the ancient mountains.\"" "<b>And from the choice produce</b> — of the eternal hills." "<b>And upon all labor of hands</b> — for it shall not succeed, and their labor is in vain; those who draw from the waters of a well shall not avail."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:24.128509455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}